return {
    ["\n　　在霍纳奇斯山脉下有一处终年被银色雾气包裹的森林，里面住着各自各样的珍稀动物。其中，有一头叫做邓恩的麋鹿住在森林的最深处，它有着云朵般柔软的灰色皮毛和比橡木还要坚实的巨大鹿角，走路时的蹄声沉稳地如同森林的呼吸。它是这座森林的守护者，拥有洞察森林每一个角落的力量，但这份力量也伴随着诅咒——每年第一场雪落下的时候，它就会开始遗忘。\n\n　　先是刚刚的对话，然后是昨天帮助过的动物，最后连自己的名字都如同飘落的雪花，落在地上了无痕迹。他只好把重要的事情都刻下来，做成木牌挂在鹿角上提醒自己。\n\n　　有一只叫戴莉的知更鸟住在森林的东边，雾气更加浓郁的地方。它有着绯红色的羽毛，它可以用歌声编织出金色的旋律，为迷路的生灵指引方向。但这里藏着它的秘密：每编织一段完整的旋律，它就会掉落一根羽毛，掉落的羽毛不会再生长。"] = "\n　　At the foot of the Hornacis Mountain Range, there is a forest covered in silver mist all year round, where all kinds of rare animals live. Among them, a moose named Dunn lives in the deepest part of the forest. It has gray fur as soft as clouds and huge antlers stronger than oak, and its hoofbeats when walking are as steady as the breathing of the forest. It is the guardian of this forest and has the power to gain insight into every corner of the forest, but this power is accompanied by a curse—when the first snow falls every year, it begins to forget.\n\n　　First, the conversation just now, then the animals it helped yesterday, and finally even its own name falls on the ground like falling snowflakes, leaving no trace. It has to carve down important things and make them into wooden signs to hang on its antlers to remind itself.\n\n　　A robin named Daly lives on the east side of the forest, where the mist is thicker. It has crimson feathers, and it can weave golden melodies with its singing to guide lost creatures. But there is a secret hidden here: every time it weaves a complete melody, it drops a feather, and the dropped feather will not grow again.",
